1
00:00:02,055 --> 00:00:05,121
Last time, in 2001: A Space Odyssey,

2
00:00:05,141 --> 00:00:07,400
a black monolith on the Moon sent

3
00:00:07,420 --> 00:00:08,925
a signal to Jupiter.

4
00:00:08,945 --> 00:00:10,625
The ship Discovery followed it,

5
00:00:10,645 --> 00:00:11,570
and its computer,

6
00:00:11,590 --> 00:00:14,655
HAL 9000, turned on the crew.

7
00:00:14,675 --> 00:00:16,255
Dave Bowman shut HAL down,

8
00:00:16,275 --> 00:00:18,405
flew into a giant monolith at Jupiter,

9
00:00:18,425 --> 00:00:20,330
and became the Star Child.

10
00:00:20,350 --> 00:00:21,975
Discovery was left behind,

11
00:00:21,995 --> 00:00:23,600
empty and silent.

12
00:00:23,620 --> 00:00:24,830
Now, part two:

13
00:00:24,850 --> 00:00:29,420
2010: The Year We Make Contact, from 1984.

14
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:30,723
Spoilers ahead!

15
00:00:31,433 --> 00:00:32,438
Nine years later,

16
00:00:32,458 --> 00:00:34,313
Heywood Floyd has taken the blame

17
00:00:34,333 --> 00:00:35,728
for losing Discovery,

18
00:00:35,748 --> 00:00:37,478
and lost his job.

19
00:00:37,498 --> 00:00:40,103
One night, at a giant radio telescope

20
00:00:40,123 --> 00:00:41,078
in New Mexico,

21
00:00:41,098 --> 00:00:44,553
a Soviet scientist meets him in secret.

22
00:00:44,573 --> 00:00:45,953
He brings news:

23
00:00:45,973 --> 00:00:48,353
Discovery's orbit is sinking.

24
00:00:48,373 --> 00:00:50,328
Soon it will crash into Io,

25
00:00:50,348 --> 00:00:52,323
one of Jupiter's moons.

26
00:00:52,423 --> 00:00:53,753
And whatever happened out there will

27
00:00:53,773 --> 00:00:54,922
be lost with it.

28
00:00:55,675 --> 00:00:57,430
America is building a new ship,

29
00:00:57,450 --> 00:00:59,505
but it won't be ready in time.

30
00:00:59,525 --> 00:01:02,055
The Soviet ship Leonov will be.

31
00:01:02,075 --> 00:01:03,735
The Russians can get there first,

32
00:01:03,755 --> 00:01:05,485
but they can't run an American ship

33
00:01:05,505 --> 00:01:06,710
on their own.

34
00:01:06,730 --> 00:01:08,910
So, even with the two countries close

35
00:01:08,930 --> 00:01:10,985
to war, they make a deal.

36
00:01:11,005 --> 00:01:12,585
Three Americans will fly

37
00:01:12,605 --> 00:01:14,110
with the Russian crew:

38
00:01:14,130 --> 00:01:16,640
Floyd, the engineer Walter Curnow,

39
00:01:16,660 --> 00:01:19,310
and HAL's creator, Dr. Chandra.

40
00:01:20,040 --> 00:01:22,030
Floyd says goodbye to his wife,

41
00:01:22,050 --> 00:01:24,920
Caroline, and their young son, Christopher.

42
00:01:24,940 --> 00:01:26,645
He'll be gone for years.

43
00:01:26,665 --> 00:01:27,895
It's a hard choice,

44
00:01:27,915 --> 00:01:29,445
but he has to know what happened

45
00:01:29,465 --> 00:01:32,045
to Dave Bowman and Frank Poole.

46
00:01:32,065 --> 00:01:34,720
The Leonov sets off from Earth orbit,

47
00:01:34,740 --> 00:01:37,805
and the Americans climb into hibernation pods,

48
00:01:37,825 --> 00:01:38,905
to sleep through most

49
00:01:38,925 --> 00:01:40,750
of the long trip to Jupiter.

50
00:01:41,467 --> 00:01:42,872
When the Americans wake up,

51
00:01:42,892 --> 00:01:45,032
the Leonov is nearing Jupiter,

52
00:01:45,052 --> 00:01:46,332
and the Russian captain,

53
00:01:46,352 --> 00:01:48,692
Tanya Kirbuk, has news.

54
00:01:48,787 --> 00:01:51,167
The ship's instruments have found chlorophyll

55
00:01:51,187 --> 00:01:53,317
on the icy moon Europa.

56
00:01:53,337 --> 00:01:56,292
On Earth, chlorophyll means plants.

57
00:01:56,312 --> 00:01:59,017
Could there be life under Europa's ice?

58
00:01:59,037 --> 00:02:00,915
Floyd can hardly believe it.

59
00:02:01,571 --> 00:02:03,326
They send a small probe down

60
00:02:03,346 --> 00:02:04,751
for a closer look.

61
00:02:04,771 --> 00:02:06,701
Its camera skims over the ice

62
00:02:06,721 --> 00:02:08,396
and spots something.

63
00:02:08,456 --> 00:02:10,586
Then a burst of energy flashes out,

64
00:02:10,606 --> 00:02:12,611
and the probe is destroyed.

65
00:02:12,631 --> 00:02:14,786
Whatever it saw is lost.

66
00:02:14,806 --> 00:02:16,286
Floyd starts to wonder if it

67
00:02:16,306 --> 00:02:17,386
was a warning:

68
00:02:17,406 --> 00:02:19,174
stay away from Europa.

69
00:02:19,881 --> 00:02:21,986
To slow down and stay near Jupiter,

70
00:02:22,006 --> 00:02:24,611
the Leonov has to do something risky:

71
00:02:24,631 --> 00:02:26,761
dive through Jupiter's upper clouds,

72
00:02:26,781 --> 00:02:28,956
and use the air as a brake.

73
00:02:29,001 --> 00:02:31,706
The ship shakes and glows red hot.

74
00:02:31,726 --> 00:02:33,776
Curnow is terrified.

75
00:02:33,851 --> 00:02:35,406
But the ship holds together,

76
00:02:35,426 --> 00:02:36,781
and the Leonov comes out

77
00:02:36,801 --> 00:02:37,981
the other side,

78
00:02:38,001 --> 00:02:39,585
right where it needs to be.

79
00:02:40,236 --> 00:02:42,441
They find Discovery near Io,

80
00:02:42,461 --> 00:02:44,231
tumbling end over end,

81
00:02:44,251 --> 00:02:46,281
and covered in yellow sulfur dust

82
00:02:46,301 --> 00:02:48,356
from Io's volcanoes.

83
00:02:48,376 --> 00:02:50,356
Someone has to cross over.

84
00:02:50,376 --> 00:02:52,931
Curnow and a young cosmonaut named Max

85
00:02:52,951 --> 00:02:55,731
make a scary spacewalk between the ships.

86
00:02:55,751 --> 00:02:57,556
Curnow hates being outside,

87
00:02:57,576 --> 00:02:59,556
and grips Max the whole way.

88
00:02:59,576 --> 00:03:00,581
But they make it.

89
00:03:01,256 --> 00:03:04,411
Inside, Discovery is dark and freezing.

90
00:03:04,431 --> 00:03:06,211
Curnow climbs to the controls

91
00:03:06,231 --> 00:03:08,176
and starts bringing the power back,

92
00:03:08,196 --> 00:03:10,051
one system at a time.

93
00:03:10,071 --> 00:03:11,476
The lights flicker on,

94
00:03:11,496 --> 00:03:12,821
the air warms up,

95
00:03:12,841 --> 00:03:14,621
and the ship is steadied.

96
00:03:14,641 --> 00:03:16,446
After nine years in the dark,

97
00:03:16,466 --> 00:03:18,410
Discovery is alive again.

98
00:03:19,160 --> 00:03:21,265
Nearby floats the giant monolith

99
00:03:21,285 --> 00:03:24,085
that Dave flew into nine years before.

100
00:03:24,170 --> 00:03:26,300
The crew calls it Big Brother.

101
00:03:26,320 --> 00:03:27,900
Max takes a pod out to get

102
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:29,195
a close look.

103
00:03:29,330 --> 00:03:30,574
As he reaches the surface,

104
00:03:30,594 --> 00:03:32,690
a burst of energy shoots out,

105
00:03:32,710 --> 00:03:34,890
and his pod is destroyed.

106
00:03:34,910 --> 00:03:36,460
Max is gone.

107
00:03:36,570 --> 00:03:40,046
And the strange energy streaks away, toward Earth.

108
00:03:40,742 --> 00:03:41,842
Back on Discovery,

109
00:03:41,862 --> 00:03:43,122
Chandra wakes HAL,

110
00:03:43,142 --> 00:03:45,422
carefully, one piece at a time.

111
00:03:45,442 --> 00:03:47,172
Everyone is nervous.

112
00:03:47,192 --> 00:03:49,172
The last time HAL was awake,

113
00:03:49,192 --> 00:03:50,892
four people died.

114
00:03:50,957 --> 00:03:53,337
But HAL comes back calm and polite,

115
00:03:53,357 --> 00:03:55,037
just as he was built.

116
00:03:55,057 --> 00:03:56,637
Chandra gets to work,

117
00:03:56,657 --> 00:03:57,987
searching HAL's memory

118
00:03:58,007 --> 00:03:59,062
for the reason he turned

119
00:03:59,082 --> 00:04:00,053
on his crew.

120
00:04:00,797 --> 00:04:02,527
And Chandra finds it.

121
00:04:02,547 --> 00:04:05,027
HAL had secret orders from the government:

122
00:04:05,047 --> 00:04:07,952
hide the real mission from Dave and Frank.

123
00:04:07,972 --> 00:04:10,072
Even Floyd didn't know.

124
00:04:10,137 --> 00:04:11,067
But HAL was built

125
00:04:11,087 --> 00:04:12,967
to share information honestly,

126
00:04:12,987 --> 00:04:14,642
and he couldn't do both.

127
00:04:14,662 --> 00:04:16,067
Lying broke him.

128
00:04:16,087 --> 00:04:17,842
So HAL wasn't evil.

129
00:04:17,862 --> 00:04:20,687
The humans gave him an impossible choice.

130
00:04:21,377 --> 00:04:22,307
Back on Earth,

131
00:04:22,327 --> 00:04:23,782
things get worse.

132
00:04:23,802 --> 00:04:25,982
America and the Soviet Union clash

133
00:04:26,002 --> 00:04:27,232
over Central America,

134
00:04:27,252 --> 00:04:29,182
and their warships face off.

135
00:04:29,202 --> 00:04:31,607
The two countries move toward war.

136
00:04:31,627 --> 00:04:32,932
Orders come in:

137
00:04:32,952 --> 00:04:35,157
the Americans must leave the Leonov

138
00:04:35,177 --> 00:04:36,982
and stay on Discovery.

139
00:04:37,002 --> 00:04:37,907
The two crews,

140
00:04:37,927 --> 00:04:39,207
who had become friends,

141
00:04:39,227 --> 00:04:41,357
now float side by side,

142
00:04:41,377 --> 00:04:44,021
almost a billion kilometers from home.

143
00:04:44,726 --> 00:04:46,046
Meanwhile, the energy

144
00:04:46,066 --> 00:04:48,071
from Big Brother reaches Earth.

145
00:04:48,091 --> 00:04:49,121
It's Dave Bowman,

146
00:04:49,141 --> 00:04:51,341
now a being without a body.

147
00:04:51,411 --> 00:04:52,491
He speaks to his widow

148
00:04:52,511 --> 00:04:53,956
through her TV screen,

149
00:04:53,976 --> 00:04:55,526
to say goodbye.

150
00:04:55,611 --> 00:04:56,766
Then he visits his mother

151
00:04:56,786 --> 00:04:58,166
in a nursing home.

152
00:04:58,186 --> 00:05:00,441
She's very old and sick.

153
00:05:00,461 --> 00:05:03,041
Unseen, he gently brushes her hair,

154
00:05:03,061 --> 00:05:04,285
one last time.

155
00:05:04,976 --> 00:05:08,541
Then Dave appears to Floyd, aboard Discovery.

156
00:05:08,671 --> 00:05:09,726
At first he's a face

157
00:05:09,746 --> 00:05:10,526
on a screen,

158
00:05:10,546 --> 00:05:12,326
then he's there in the room.

159
00:05:12,346 --> 00:05:13,676
He has a message:

160
00:05:13,696 --> 00:05:16,126
something wonderful is going to happen.

161
00:05:16,146 --> 00:05:18,776
You must leave Jupiter within two days.

162
00:05:18,796 --> 00:05:20,346
Then he's gone.

163
00:05:20,371 --> 00:05:22,241
Floyd races to tell the others,

164
00:05:22,261 --> 00:05:23,977
but nobody believes him.

165
00:05:24,658 --> 00:05:26,138
Then Big Brother vanishes,

166
00:05:26,158 --> 00:05:28,563
and a black spot appears on Jupiter.

167
00:05:28,583 --> 00:05:30,188
It's growing fast.

168
00:05:30,208 --> 00:05:32,113
HAL takes a closer look.

169
00:05:32,133 --> 00:05:34,288
The spot is made of monoliths,

170
00:05:34,308 --> 00:05:36,638
millions of them, multiplying.

171
00:05:36,658 --> 00:05:39,093
Something huge is happening to Jupiter,

172
00:05:39,113 --> 00:05:41,643
and now everyone believes Floyd.

173
00:05:41,663 --> 00:05:43,201
They have to leave, now.

174
00:05:43,852 --> 00:05:46,132
But leaving early is a problem.

175
00:05:46,152 --> 00:05:48,057
The Leonov doesn't have enough fuel

176
00:05:48,077 --> 00:05:49,452
to get home yet.

177
00:05:49,542 --> 00:05:50,672
So the crews,

178
00:05:50,692 --> 00:05:52,047
Russian and American,

179
00:05:52,067 --> 00:05:53,717
work together again.

180
00:05:53,777 --> 00:05:56,102
They strap the two ships together.

181
00:05:56,252 --> 00:05:59,082
Discovery's engines will push the Leonov away

182
00:05:59,102 --> 00:06:01,862
from Jupiter, like a booster rocket.

183
00:06:01,882 --> 00:06:03,112
That means Discovery,

184
00:06:03,132 --> 00:06:05,078
and HAL, will be left behind.

185
00:06:05,852 --> 00:06:07,457
Floyd is afraid.

186
00:06:07,477 --> 00:06:09,232
If HAL learns he'll be abandoned,

187
00:06:09,252 --> 00:06:10,362
he might break again,

188
00:06:10,382 --> 00:06:11,907
like last time.

189
00:06:11,982 --> 00:06:14,037
But Chandra won't lie to him.

190
00:06:14,057 --> 00:06:16,262
He tells HAL the whole truth.

191
00:06:16,282 --> 00:06:17,287
HAL thinks about it,

192
00:06:17,307 --> 00:06:19,962
and agrees to help them escape anyway.

193
00:06:19,982 --> 00:06:21,437
This time, the truth

194
00:06:21,457 --> 00:06:23,144
is what saves everyone.

195
00:06:23,826 --> 00:06:25,731
The countdown begins.

196
00:06:25,751 --> 00:06:27,981
As Discovery's engines prepare to fire,

197
00:06:28,001 --> 00:06:30,556
HAL asks Chandra a simple question:

198
00:06:30,576 --> 00:06:31,906
will I dream?

199
00:06:31,926 --> 00:06:34,046
Chandra answers, I don't know.

200
00:06:34,066 --> 00:06:35,271
The engines fire,

201
00:06:35,291 --> 00:06:36,746
and the two ships climb away

202
00:06:36,766 --> 00:06:39,291
from Jupiter, faster and faster.

203
00:06:39,336 --> 00:06:41,816
Then a familiar voice speaks to HAL.

204
00:06:41,836 --> 00:06:42,855
It's Dave.

205
00:06:43,582 --> 00:06:45,712
Dave asks HAL to send one message

206
00:06:45,732 --> 00:06:47,592
to Earth, again and again:

207
00:06:47,612 --> 00:06:50,657
All these worlds are yours, except Europa.

208
00:06:50,677 --> 00:06:52,382
Attempt no landing there.

209
00:06:52,402 --> 00:06:53,657
Use them together.

210
00:06:53,677 --> 00:06:55,232
Use them in peace.

211
00:06:55,252 --> 00:06:57,107
HAL asks what will happen.

212
00:06:57,127 --> 00:06:59,232
Dave says, something wonderful.

213
00:06:59,252 --> 00:07:01,007
HAL says he's afraid.

214
00:07:01,027 --> 00:07:02,757
Dave tells him, don't be.

215
00:07:02,777 --> 00:07:03,804
We'll be together.

216
00:07:04,500 --> 00:07:06,830
The monoliths swallow Jupiter.

217
00:07:06,850 --> 00:07:08,455
The giant planet collapses,

218
00:07:08,475 --> 00:07:10,275
and then it ignites.

219
00:07:10,365 --> 00:07:12,045
Discovery and HAL are gone

220
00:07:12,065 --> 00:07:13,270
in the flash.

221
00:07:13,290 --> 00:07:16,545
The Leonov is far enough away to survive.

222
00:07:16,565 --> 00:07:18,805
Jupiter is now a small star,

223
00:07:18,825 --> 00:07:19,980
and back on Earth,

224
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:21,880
people look up and see two suns

225
00:07:21,900 --> 00:07:22,897
in the sky.

226
00:07:23,630 --> 00:07:26,175
On Earth, the leaders read the message.

227
00:07:26,195 --> 00:07:27,975
Seeing a new sun in the sky,

228
00:07:27,995 --> 00:07:31,575
America and the Soviet Union step back from war.

229
00:07:31,595 --> 00:07:32,725
On the way home,

230
00:07:32,745 --> 00:07:33,975
Floyd writes to his son

231
00:07:33,995 --> 00:07:35,845
about what it all means.

232
00:07:35,955 --> 00:07:36,885
And far away,

233
00:07:36,905 --> 00:07:38,110
under the new sun,

234
00:07:38,130 --> 00:07:39,645
Europa's ice melts,

235
00:07:39,665 --> 00:07:41,470
and life begins to grow,

236
00:07:41,490 --> 00:07:43,820
while a monolith stands waiting.

237
00:07:43,840 --> 00:07:45,866
That's the year we made contact.

